# One line ending, everywhere.
#
# Git was handing this checkout CRLF on Windows while CI read LF, so code that
# read a file — the exclusions twin parser, the stylesheets inlined into every
# route page — behaved differently on the machine the human walks from than in
# the pipeline. Two gates were green in CI and red here before this line
# (2026-09-10). Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every
# platform; the parsers stay defensive, but they no longer carry the product
# alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Every TypeScript file diffs as text, whatever is inside it.
#
# `sliceFingerprint` in src/watch/core.ts joins a slice's two markers with a
# NUL, so the file contains one — and `text=auto` above classifies a file with
# a NUL as binary. `git diff` printed "Bin 23400 -> 29550 bytes" for it: the
# one file that decides how every source is read could not be reviewed in a
# diff or in a pull request, and s34 changed 122 lines of it invisibly
# (2026-09-23). This says only how to DISPLAY the file; it stores no different
# bytes and `eol=lf` above still governs the line endings.
*.ts diff
